Note: The given code is a recursive implementation of the Fibonacci sequence, which will result in a time complexity of O(2^n) and will not be suitable for large inputs.

To compute the Fibonacci sequence for a given input in a non-recursive approach, we can use an iterative method. We will use a loop to calculate the Fibonacci numbers iteratively, keeping track of the last two numbers in the sequence.

Here is the corrected code:

