The then method adds the callback function to the thenCallbacks array and checks if the promise has already been resolved. If it has, it immediately runs the callback function. It returns the same customPromise object to allow chaining.

The catch method is similar to the then method but adds the callback function to the catchCallbacks array.

The finally method sets the finallyCallback and runs it if the promise has already been resolved or rejected.

The delay method adds a delay before invoking the resolve or reject callbacks using the setTimeout function. It returns a new customPromise object with the same then, catch, finally, and delay methods to allow chaining.

